{
  "slug": "brandketing",
  "name": "Brandketing",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Marketing intelligence plugin that builds a living context store from product docs, customer calls, CRM data, and competitor research - then compiles structured briefs and generates copy through a 6-step strategy workflow with a built-in critic pass. Separates evidence collection, human approval, brief compilation, and copy generation into distinct steps so the model never does extraction, positioning, and writing in one jump.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**, **4 agents** and **5 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `compile` (This skill should be used when assembling a marketing brief from approved context store objects, mapping object types…), `critique` (This skill should be used when red-teaming marketing copy, auditing for failure modes, rewriting weak lines, or when…), `generate` (This skill should be used when running the 6-step marketing strategy workflow, generating copy hierarchies from a brief,…), `ingest` (This skill should be used when ingesting raw marketing sources into the brandketing context store, normalizing content into…)\n- **Agents** (4): `compiler` (Assembles a structured marketing brief from approved context store objects), `critic` (Red-teams marketing copy output from the strategist agent), `normalizer` (Converts raw source files into structured context store objects (Capability, Pain, Quote, UseCase, Persona, Competitor, Cliche, Proof)), `strategist` (Runs the 6-step marketing strategy workflow to produce a full copy hierarchy from a compiled brief)\n- **Commands** (5): `brief` (Compile a marketing brief from approved context store objects), `generate` (Generate marketing copy from the context store or a provided brief), `ingest` (Ingest a raw source file into the context store by normalizing it into structured objects), `review` (Review and approve/reject pending objects in the context store), `status` (Show the current state of the context store - object counts, approval status, and freshness by layer)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install brandketing@claude-community` from `entro314-labs/brandketing`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
